#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1319 expect=noViolation domain=DS
#note "dataset DS without the DSSTDTC column (plus the DM block). The lead `not empty(--STDTC)` over the absent column broadcast-folds to FALSE -> SILENT noViolation WITH execution - no skip, because SD1319 (unlike SD1202 and unlike its own FDA twin) authors no Requirements.Variables gate. *** This is the single named FLIP FIXTURE for finding SD1319-F1: if the lane accepts the proposed `Requirements.Variables.All: [--STDTC]`, re-pin this scenario to expect=skipped - one edit, nothing else moves. Pins TODAY'S behaviour per the K2-05 precedent; deliberately NOT a D9 red. ***"
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset DS class=EVENTS
col STUDYID type=Char
col DOMAIN  type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col DSSEQ   type=Num
col DSDECOD type=Char
---
S1 | DS | 001 | 1 | RANDOMIZED
---

dataset DM class="SPECIAL PURPOSE"
col STUDYID  type=Char
col DOMAIN   type=Char
col USUBJID  type=Char
col RFICDTC  type=Char
---
S1 | DM | 001 | 2020-01-01
